    {
      "id": "SA-C27-so-be-it",
      "sequence": 1280,
      "title": "अस्तु (astu) — so be it, all right",
      "headword": "अस्तु",
      "romanization": "astu",
      "gloss": "so be it, all right",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:137d52e986142828",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new word: what did vaidyaḥ mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अस्तु",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अस्तु (astu) — \"so be it, all right\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have had आम् and न for yes and no since the first chapter, and they are blunt. अस्तु (astu) is the agreeable middle: let it be so, all right, fine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is not a new word so much as a new face on one you know. अस्ति (asti), \"is\", was the third person of the root as, \"to be\". अस्तु (astu) is the same verb in the commanding form: let it be. Sanskrit answers a request by ordering the world to comply."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A reply softer than yes, built out of the be-verb you already had."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "astu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *astu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "asti, then astu, and say what changed between them",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *asti*, then *astu*, and say what changed between them]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say hastaḥ, then read गुरुः",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *hastaḥ*, then read **गुरुः**]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does अस्तु (astu) mean? (\"so be it, all right\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "SA-S223-vowel-sign-ai",
      "sequence": 1281,
      "title": "◌ै (ai) — one character, met inside words you already say",
      "headword": "ै",
      "romanization": "ai",
      "gloss": "the single character ◌ै — recognised inside words you already say",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "pen",
      "derivedModality": "pen",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "writing-type",
        "writing-block",
        "script-block"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:f221cfaab324525c",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "pen",
        "needs": [
          "a pen and something to write on",
          "your eyes, for letter shapes on the page"
        ],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Script you'll notice: ◌ै",
          "Guided Practice"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your hands, so it is not a driving lesson. You will want a pen and something to write on and your eyes, for letter shapes on the page. You can listen to everything else now — leave the sections called Script you'll notice: ◌ै and Guided Practice until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one, the ones you have already met: ◌ू, ओ, फ. Say what each of them does."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One character this time. One only — and you have been saying it for pages without knowing which mark on the page it was."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "script",
          "title": "Script you'll notice: ◌ै",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "◌ै — ai."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is a vowel sign. It is not a letter and never stands alone: it attaches to a consonant and replaces the a built into it. Replaces, not adds — the a is gone."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Where it sits: a double stroke above the top bar."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Worked through: न + ◌ै = नै — nai."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You already say these, and every one of them has ◌ै (ai) somewhere inside it:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वैद्यः vaidyaḥ — a physician."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing: ◌ै — copy what you see",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Put your pen on ◌ै (ai) and follow its line. Copy the shape you can see — slowly, and larger than it is printed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This book does not yet tell you where to start the character or which way to travel. That is a real thing, taught with real variation from school to school, and it is not written down here until it can be written down with a source. Copying what is in front of you needs no such source, and it is how the shape gets into your hand in the meantime."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "at this, and find ◌ै (ai) in it",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: at this, and find ◌ै in it]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वैद्यः."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "TRACE",
              "instruction": "◌ै three times, saying ai as you finish each one",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU TRACE: ◌ै three times, saying *ai* as you finish each one]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "LOOK",
              "instruction": "back at any page of this chapter and find ◌ै (ai) once more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU LOOK: back at any page of this chapter and find ◌ै once more]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which character is this — ◌ै? What vowel does it put on the consonant it attaches to — and what does it take off? (Puts ai on; takes the built-in a off.) Name one word you already say that contains it."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
