        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: सत्यम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सत्यम् (satyam) — \"true; the truth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सत्यम् answers a claim: true. As a noun it is the truth, and it is the word on the national emblem of India — satyam eva jayate, \"truth alone conquers\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Look at what it is made of. Sat- is the being-form of that same root as you met in अस्ति and अस्तु (astu): what is. Add an ending and truth is simply the state of being what is. English has a cousin, well hidden: sooth, as in soothsayer — a truth-sayer — and forsooth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A third word from the be-verb, and truth defined as what is."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
